<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <LangVersion>preview</LangVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="Ticker.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Program.fs" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- No product dependency pulls FSharp.Core in as copy-local for a
         package-free console app; without this the built binary can't find
         it at run time even though it compiles fine. -->
    <PackageReference Include="FSharp.Core" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The counter below is held in a REGISTERED holder, which is what makes
         the app's live state visible to a hot-reload restart.

         A USER NEEDS NOTHING HERE. When SageFs builds this project — the Run
         App path, any session rebuild, a cold restart — it injects its own
         reference itself (`SessionBuild.prepareCoreReference` writes a
         .targets and passes -p:CustomAfterMicrosoftCommonTargets), so the
         holder API resolves with no Reference in this file. Proven end to end
         on a project with zero Reference elements.

         This Reference exists for ONE case: CI builds the samples with a raw
         `dotnet build` (ci-pipeline.fsx "build samples for integration suites"),
         which is not a SageFs build and therefore gets no injection. It resolves
         the assembly from `$(SageFsCoreAssembly)`, defined in the repo-root
         Directory.Build.props and guarded by Exists so a machine that has never
         built Core just gets no Reference at all.

         A ProjectReference is NOT an option here, and that was measured: it
         pulls FSharp.Core 11.0.101-preview7.26381.103 transitively through
         FSharp.Compiler.Service, which this sample's own pinned FSharp.Core
         (…26359.118) reads as a downgrade, and the repo treats warnings as
         errors. Do not "simplify" this into one. -->
    <Reference Include="SageFs.Core" Condition="'$(SageFsCoreAssembly)' != ''">
      <HintPath>$(SageFsCoreAssembly)</HintPath>
      <Private>true</Private>
    </Reference>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
